464	    split the category into separate awards for dramatic scores and comedy/musical scores; this dataset presents one
465	    consolidated winner per ceremony year. The 93 winning scores represent <strong>{kpi_total_unique} distinct composers</strong>
466	    (counting individuals within shared awards) and <strong>{len(set(r['film'] for r in rows))} unique films</strong>.
467	  </p>
468	  <p>
469	    The composer pool reveals a striking concentration: <strong>{kpi_repeat_rate}%</strong> of all ceremonies were won by a composer
470	    who had already claimed the award at least once before. A handful of names appear again and again across the decades,
471	    while many composers appear just once — a testament to both the towering dominance of certain figures and the category's
472	    capacity to recognize new voices.
