    The Academy Award for Best Original Score has been awarded at 93 ceremonies spanning from the 6th Academy Awards
    in 1934 through the 98th ceremony in March 2026. This dataset consolidates every winner into a single canonical record,
    tracing the evolution of film music's highest honor across nine decades.
  </p>
  <p>
    The award category has undergone several name changes and structural shifts across its history. In certain years, the Academy
    split the category into separate awards for dramatic scores and comedy/musical scores; this dataset presents one
    consolidated winner per ceremony year. The 93 winning scores represent <strong>{kpi_total_unique} distinct composers</strong>
    (counting individuals within shared awards) and <strong>{len(set(r['film'] for r in rows))} unique films</strong>.
  </p>
  <p>
