    who had already claimed the award at least once before ({repeat_years} out of {len(rows)} ceremonies).
    A small number of names appear again and again across the decades — three composers are tied at {kpi_max_wins} wins each —
    while the majority of the {kpi_total_unique} winners have won exactly once, a testament to both towering individual
    dominance and the category's capacity to recognize new voices.
  </p>

  <div class="data-note">
    <strong>Data Quality Note:</strong> The dataset contains one anomaly: <em>Oppenheimer</em> appears as the winner
