<!-- ═══════════ SECTION 3: TEMPORAL PATTERNS ═══════════ -->
<section id="temporal-patterns">
  <h2>3. Temporal Patterns &amp; Decade-by-Decade Breakdown</h2>
  <p>
    The distribution of awards across decades reveals distinct patterns of concentration and diversity.
    Some decades were defined by a small set of repeat winners; others saw the award spread across a broad field
    of composers, reflecting shifts in the industry, scoring technology, and Academy voting behavior.
  </p>
  <p>
    The <strong>{kpi_best_decade_str}</strong> share the record for most unique winners in a decade,
    with <strong>{kpi_best_decade_count}</strong> distinct composers each. By contrast, the 1950s produced only
    <strong>{decade_stats['1950s']['unique_winners']}</strong> unique winners across 10 ceremonies — the lowest
